  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Lovesac is navigating a contracting home-furnishings market, yet it is capturing modest market share. A record wave of new product launches is imminent, aimed at reinforcing its living-room position across small‑, medium‑, and large‑format Sactionals. While industry headwinds keep top‑line gains slight, structural improvements are quietly transforming profitability: gross margins are expanding meaningfully, demonstrating that operating leverage exists even in a soft demand environment.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is prioritizing disciplined cost control and margin expansion over near‑term revenue growth. A fortified, debt‑free balance sheet supports strategic initiatives, including a planned U.S. manufacturing shift intended to lock in sustainably higher margins. Guidance was refined cautiously, balancing macro prudence with conviction in the upcoming innovation cadence. The market, which has often dismissed the company as a chronic underperformer, is now being confronted with a credible margin‑inflection narrative driven by steady execution.",
